From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 07:53:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: apple-soc: Require a governor that drives the zone's
 cooling device

A zone counts as the board thermal policy when the cluster's cpufreq
cooling device is bound to one of its passive trips. Binding alone does
not make the zone act. Device-tree zones get the default governor, and
the arm64 asahi.config the Omarchy recipe merges selects
THERMAL_DEFAULT_GOV_POWER_ALLOCATOR. The power allocator only drives
cooling devices with a power model; the T8132 OPP tables carry no
opp-microwatt and the CPUs no dynamic-power-coefficient, so no energy
model is registered and the cpufreq cooling devices are not power
actors. Under that governor the passive trips never throttle, yet the
zone owner would lift the P-state cap.

Add thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev() to the thermal core. It answers
from an allowlist, under the zone lock: true for step_wise and
fair_share, and for power_allocator only if the cooling device is a
power actor; false for bang_bang, which only ever requests state 0 or 1
and so moves a multi-state cpufreq device by one OPP at most, for
user_space, for unknown or out-of-tree governors, for a zone without a
governor, and for a zone that is not enabled or not ready (disabled,
suspended, resuming, initialising or going away), since such a zone
runs no governor.

apple_zone_check() treats a zone whose governor would leave the
policy's cooling device alone as not usable (-EOPNOTSUPP). The owner
runs that check on every 500 ms sample, so the cap stays until the zone
runs a governor that acts, for example after
"echo step_wise > /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zoneN/policy"; ownership
is taken after the usual good samples and given back after two bad
ones if the governor is switched away or the zone disabled again.

The helper matches governor names with strcmp(). That keeps the change
self-contained but is fragile; a governor operation such as
bool (*drives_cdev)(tz, cdev) would be the cleaner interface to
propose upstream.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c |  7 ++++-
 drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c      | 44 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/thermal.h             |  5 ++++
 3 files changed, 55 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
index af9e8758ac..6efb44fe2d 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
@@ -1345,7 +1345,9 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_soc_cpufreq_set_thermal_owner);
  *
  *  - be registered and read a temperature of at least APPLE_ZONE_MIN_MC and
  *    below its hot trip,
- *  - have the policy's cpufreq cooling device bound to a passive trip, and
+ *  - be enabled and have the policy's cpufreq cooling device bound to a
+ *    passive trip, with a governor that drives it over its whole range
+ *    (step_wise, fair_share, or power_allocator with an energy model), and
  *  - have a hot trip above the lowest such passive trip and a critical trip
  *    at or above the hot trip.
  *
@@ -1464,6 +1466,9 @@ static int apple_zone_check(struct device_node *zone,
 	ret = thermal_zone_get_temp(c.tz, temp);
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = for_each_thermal_trip(c.tz, apple_zone_check_trip, &c);
+	/* A trip the governor ignores protects nothing. */
+	if (!ret && !thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev(c.tz, cdev))
+		ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	thermal_zone_put(c.tz);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
diff --git a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
index fb6c5804ae..1fb8c74342 100644
--- a/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/thermal_core.c
@@ -1735,6 +1735,50 @@ void thermal_zone_put(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(thermal_zone_put);
 
+/**
+ * thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev() - will the zone's governor drive @cdev?
+ * @tz: thermal zone
+ * @cdev: a cooling device bound to trips of @tz
+ *
+ * Binding a cooling device to a trip does not make the zone's governor act on
+ * it. The power allocator governor only drives cooling devices that have a
+ * power model and leaves any other bound cooling device in its lowest state,
+ * bang-bang only ever requests state 0 or 1, the user space governor drives
+ * none, and a zone that is disabled, suspended or going away runs no governor
+ * at all. A driver that relies on a zone's passive trips for protection can
+ * use this to check that they act.
+ *
+ * The answer is an allowlist: governors not known to step a multi-state
+ * cooling device through its range, including out-of-tree ones, give false.
+ * It reflects the zone at the time of the call; callers that depend on it
+ * must re-check periodically.
+ *
+ * Return: true if @tz is enabled and ready and its current governor drives
+ * @cdev over its full state range.
+ */
+bool thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev(struct thermal_zone_device *tz,
+				      struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev)
+{
+	const char *name;
+
+	guard(thermal_zone)(tz);
+
+	if (tz->mode != THERMAL_DEVICE_ENABLED || tz->state != TZ_STATE_READY)
+		return false;
+	/* No fallback to the default governor: be conservative. */
+	if (!tz->governor)
+		return false;
+
+	/* Matching on names keeps this self-contained; see the changelog. */
+	name = tz->governor->name;
+	if (!strcmp(name, "step_wise") || !strcmp(name, "fair_share"))
+		return true;
+	if (!strcmp(name, "power_allocator"))
+		return cdev_is_power_actor(cdev);
+	return false;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev);
+
 /**
  * thermal_zone_get_temp_by_name() - sample a uniquely named registered zone
  * @name: thermal zone name
diff --git a/include/linux/thermal.h b/include/linux/thermal.h
index fed4a76cff..b4250b868a 100644
--- a/include/linux/thermal.h
+++ b/include/linux/thermal.h
@@ -305,6 +305,8 @@ void thermal_cooling_device_unregister(struct thermal_cooling_device *);
 struct thermal_zone_device *thermal_zone_get_zone_by_name(const char *name);
 struct thermal_zone_device *thermal_zone_get_by_name(const char *name);
 void thermal_zone_put(struct thermal_zone_device *tz);
+bool thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev(struct thermal_zone_device *tz,
+				      struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev);
 int thermal_zone_get_temp(struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp);
 int thermal_zone_get_temp_by_name(const char *name, int *temp);
 int thermal_zone_get_slope(struct thermal_zone_device *tz);
@@ -364,6 +366,9 @@ static inline struct thermal_zone_device *thermal_zone_get_by_name(
 { return ERR_PTR(-ENODEV); }
 static inline void thermal_zone_put(struct thermal_zone_device *tz)
 { }
+static inline bool thermal_zone_governor_moves_cdev(
+		struct thermal_zone_device *tz, struct thermal_cooling_device *cdev)
+{ return false; }
 static inline int thermal_zone_get_temp(
 		struct thermal_zone_device *tz, int *temp)
 { return -ENODEV; }
